From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:06:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sb/intel/lynxpoint: Fix OC mapping of USB2 ports 8 to 13

On LPT-H, USB2 ports 8 to 13 are mapped to the OC4 to OC7 pins through
EHCI2 OCMAP and xHCI U2OCM2. Each OC pin has one byte in these
registers, with bit 0 for port 8. The native USB init uses the port
index itself as bit offset, like for ports 0 to 7, so every port lands
in the byte of the next OC pin, and OC7 cannot be mapped at all (the
shift check rejects it). On the W541, for example, OCMAP becomes
0x300c0300 instead of 0x00300c03.

Use the port index relative to port 8, as bd82x6x does for its second
EHCI controller.

TEST=Built for lenovo/w541. Not tested on hardware yet.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_usb_native.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_usb_native.c b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_usb_native.c
index b63ae3d50..ff167fa1c 100644
--- a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_usb_native.c
+++ b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_usb_native.c
@@ -402,7 +402,7 @@ static void usb_overcurrent_mapping(void)
 		}
 		/* Ports 8 .. 13 => OC 4 .. 7 (LPT-H only) */
 		if (!is_lp && idx >= 8 && oc_pin >= 4) {
-			const int shift = PORT_TO_OC_SHIFT(idx, oc_pin - 4);
+			const int shift = PORT_TO_OC_SHIFT(idx - 8, oc_pin - 4);
 			if (shift_ok(shift)) {
 				printk(BIOS_DEBUG, "mapped to OC pin %u\n", oc_pin);
 				ehci_2_ocmap |= 1 << shift;
-- 
